      "title": "14.8.1 Factors affecting air quality",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 314,
          "pdf_to": 315,
          "note": "Topic 14.8.1 as printed, with Table 14.2 printed at its end, printed pages 314-315. The print numbers the factors i, ii, iv, v."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Air quality is influenced by several key factors or sources."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "i) Emission sources"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Burning of wood and fossil fuels can increase local pollution level. Factories and power plants use fossil fuels that release dangerous pollutants in air like SOₓ and NOₓ. Vehicles release CO, PM and VOCs."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "ii) Meteorological conditions"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Wind, temperature, and humidity affect pollutant dispersion and concentration. A layer of warm air trapping pollutants near the ground can lead to poor air quality."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "iv) Natural Events"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Wild fires can release large amounts of smoke and PM into the atmosphere. Natural dust storms can significantly lower air quality."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "v) Seasonal Changes"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Temperature variations, such as heating or cooling of buildings in different seasons can increase emissions of pollutants. Seasonal pollen concentration can contribute to poor air quality."
          },
          {
